    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The investment plan calls for a Hold, and the evidence supports this balanced stance. JPM is in a confirmed uptrend above all key moving averages (10 EMA, 50 SMA, 200 SMA) with strong balance sheet fundamentals ($327.9B equity, +$55B net cash build in FY2023), but the technicals are stretched \u2014 RSI at 74.15 rolling over from 78.01, MACD histogram contracting, and the stock trading 21.4% above its 200-day SMA. The near-term risk-reward is poor (roughly 1.3% upside to the upper Bollinger Band vs 3-6% downside to 20/50 SMA support), and critically, there is no income statement data available to validate the earnings power thesis. The plan's strategic guidance is to maintain the current position without adding new exposure at $175.81, consider trimming 10-20% into strength near the $178 upper Bollinger Band, and establish a re-entry plan in the $164-$170 accumulation zone if a pullback occurs.\n\n**Stop Loss**: 164.86\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain current position; consider trimming 10-20% into strength near $178; re-enter/add in the $164-$170 zone\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
